From 88e94b39bff033d04060fc13a65823250c350ccd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:08:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 235/235] media: i2c: lc898214xd: expose the lens travel the
 servo actually has

FOCUS_ABSOLUTE spanned hall +324..-257, taken from the vendor's
af_tuning region params on the assumption that they bounded the
mechanism. They do not.

Commanding the target register directly and reading the hall sensor
back shows the servo tracking to within a few counts across a far wider
span:

  commanded  268   324   500   700   900  1112  1400
  hall       267   333   503   702   899  1110  1335

1112 is this module's OTP macro code and the servo lands on it; only
near 1400 does it lag into the mechanical stop.

What the old range cost: with exposure, scene stability and the
actuator readback all held, a subject at 0.222 m focuses sharply at
hall ~530 -- a 13x sharpness peak, and about 200 counts past anything
the control could command. Nothing nearer than roughly 0.6 m could be
focused at all; a sweep at 0.155 m stayed flat to within 5% with no
peak anywhere, and subjects at 0.47 m and 0.57 m pinned against the end
stop. That is the whole of "autofocus does not work" on this device.

So expose 0..1369 onto hall -257..+1112, which also puts the control
the way round V4L2 specifies: higher means nearer.

These bounds are the span this part was verified to track, not a
calibration. Where infinity and macro fall inside it belongs to the
individual module and stays in userspace tuning data; libcamera's
dioptre map moves with this commit and the two must land together.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
 drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c | 68 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c b/drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c
index f71475a423d3..1ea33349343c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c
@@ -85,39 +85,51 @@
  * signed: infinity 0x144 = +324, macro 0x0eff = -257 (libactuator_lc898214xd.so
  * .data, and .data+0x1808 for initial_code).
  *
- * V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE is unsigned and, by convention, increases towards
- * near focus. So expose 0..581, mapping 0 -> +324 (infinity) and 581 -> -257
- * (macro), and convert on the way to the hardware.
+ * Those two af_tuning fields do NOT bound the mechanism, and taking them as
+ * the range made close focus impossible. Measured 2026-09-16 by commanding
+ * the target register directly (bringup/camera/vcm-poke.py) and reading the
+ * hall sensor back:
+ *
+ *   commanded  268   324   500   700   900  1112  1400
+ *   hall       267   333   503   702   899  1110  1335
  *
- * UNRESOLVED, measured 2026-09-16 (bringup/camera/af-sweep.py, exposure and
- * scene stability both held, actuator readback tracking every step):
+ * The servo tracks to within a few counts all the way to 1112 -- which is
+ * exactly this module's OTP macro code -- and only lags approaching 1400 as
+ * it reaches the mechanical stop. So the travel runs from roughly -257 to
+ * about +1335, and af_tuning's "infinity 324 / macro -257" describes a narrow
+ * slice on the FAR side of it.
  *
- *   subject                 distance   sharpest at
- *   lit book, square on     0.47 m     code 0    (9.3x over the range)
- *   room, shelving          ~2-3 m     code 128  (up to 11x)
- *   book on a far shelf     far        code 192  (15.5x)
+ * What that cost, measured with the same sweep and all of exposure, scene
+ * stability and actuator readback held (bringup/camera/af-sweep.py): a
+ * subject at 0.222 m focuses sharply at hall ~530, a 13x sharpness peak. The
+ * old range topped out at +324, so no subject nearer than roughly 0.6 m could
+ * be focused at all -- a sweep at 0.155 m stayed flat to within 5% with no
+ * peak anywhere, and subjects at 0.47 m and 0.57 m both pinned against the
+ * end stop.
+ *
+ * V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE is unsigned and, by convention, increases towards
+ * near focus. So expose 0..1369 mapping onto hall -257..+1112, which finally
+ * puts this control the way round V4L2 specifies.
  *
- * Sharpness rises with distance as the CODE rises, so pos 0 focuses NEAR and
- * pos 581 FAR -- the opposite of both the labels above and the V4L2
- * convention. A fit through the two solid points puts infinity near code 157,
- * which would leave roughly two thirds of the exposed range beyond infinity
- * and the near end unreachable (a subject at 0.155 m stayed flat to within
- * 5% across the whole sweep, with no peak anywhere).
+ * The bounds below are the span this part was verified to track, not a
+ * calibration: where infinity and macro actually fall within it is a property
+ * of the individual module (its OTP says 268 and 1112 here), and belongs in
+ * userspace tuning data rather than in this driver. libcamera's dioptre-to-
+ * code map is where that lives, and it has to be updated whenever this range
+ * changes.
  *
- * That cannot be reconciled with the vendor's af_tuning (infinity +324, macro
- * -257) without either those two fields being read swapped out of
- * libactuator_lc898214xd.so, or the hall scale not being the DAC scale. The
- * polarity is deliberately NOT flipped here yet: the tuning file's dioptre
- * map would have to move in the same commit, and the fit needs stations at
- * measured distances in daylight first.
+ * Known follow-up: a blind contrast scan now spends its first ~38% of travel
+ * beyond infinity, where nothing changes. Seeding the scan from the module's
+ * calibration (or from the laser rangefinder) is the fix for that; shrinking
+ * this range to suit one module is not.
  */
-#define LC898214XD_CODE_INFINITY	324
-#define LC898214XD_CODE_MACRO		(-257)
+#define LC898214XD_CODE_FAR		(-257)
+#define LC898214XD_CODE_NEAR		1112
 #define LC898214XD_POS_MIN		0
-#define LC898214XD_POS_MAX		(LC898214XD_CODE_INFINITY - LC898214XD_CODE_MACRO)
+#define LC898214XD_POS_MAX		(LC898214XD_CODE_NEAR - LC898214XD_CODE_FAR)
 
-/* Vendor af_tuning initial_code is the macro end. */
-#define LC898214XD_POS_DEFAULT		LC898214XD_POS_MAX
+/* Park at the far end: a frame focused past infinity beats one at macro. */
+#define LC898214XD_POS_DEFAULT		LC898214XD_POS_MIN
 
 struct lc898214xd {
 	struct v4l2_subdev sd;
@@ -179,8 +191,8 @@ static int lc898214xd_set_pos(struct lc898214xd *lens, u16 pos)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* 0 = infinity, POS_MAX = macro; the hardware code runs the other way. */
-	code = LC898214XD_CODE_INFINITY - pos;
+	/* 0 = far, POS_MAX = near; the hardware code runs the same way. */
+	code = LC898214XD_CODE_FAR + pos;
 
 	return i2c_smbus_write_word_swapped(lens->client, LC898214XD_REG_TARGET,
 					    (u16)(code << LC898214XD_CODE_SHIFT));
